invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_word.h
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: the square of four words leaves out the carry into its top word,
  so a square whose chain of the four a_i^2 carried there is short by
  2^448. Nothing faults: uint64_t arithmetic defines every wrap, and the
  field's square and the scalar inverse's squarings go on computing with a
  wrong value. bin/p256_equiv_test holds every square to p256_field.c's
  and every inverse to p256_field.c's and p256_scalar.c's.

--- old
    *t7 = d7 + (uint64_t)(q3 >> 64) + carry;
--- new
    (void)carry;
    *t7 = d7 + (uint64_t)(q3 >> 64);
